{
  "name": "leafy",
  "description": "leafy is a minimalist Lua-based hierarchical router that utilizes recursive table traversal and metatable-driven defaults to resolve URI-style paths into callable handlers. It implements a flexible dispatch protocol where path segments are mapped to table keys, supporting dynamic capture and nested routing through a state-aware default lookup mechanism. The library is designed as a zero-dependency primitive for high-performance Lua applications requiring predictable and extensible request routing.",
